\section{Known upstream gotcha}{

Pandoc's docx writer wraps every \verb{#}-heading section in body-level
\code{bookmarkStart}/\code{bookmarkEnd} markers (siblings of \verb{<w:p>}, not nested in
one). \code{reportifyr}'s own \code{build_report()} -> \code{validate_alt_text_magic_strings()}
assumes the paragraph right after any \verb{\{rpfy\}:} magic string is itself a
\verb{<w:p>}, and crashes with an \code{lxml} "Undefined namespace prefix" error if a
magic string is the very last thing in a section (the "next paragraph" it
finds is actually that trailing bookmarkEnd, or the closing \verb{<w:sectPr>} at
the end of the whole document). Put at least one line of real content (a
sentence, a footnote lead-in, anything) after the last magic string in
each section to avoid this -- confirmed via a real end-to-end render.
}

